  "result": "The `wire` package is implemented in `wire/codec.py` and all 6 tests pass.\n\nI chose **Approach A (compact binary)**. Fixed-width `struct` records give exact IEEE-754 round trips for NaN and -0.0 without any special casing, and a header record count plus a CRC32 trailer make truncation and corruption detection precise and cheap.\n\n**Format details:**\n- Header: 4-byte magic `WIRE`, version byte, u32 record count.\n- Records: 15 bytes each, big-endian `ts u32 | sensor_id u16 | flags u8 | value f64`.\n- Footer: CRC32 over header and body.\n\n`decode` raises `CodecError` on bad magic, unsupported version, truncated or oversized input, and checksum mismatch. `encode` also validates field names, types, and integer ranges before packing. Nothing is committed yet. The only new file is `wire/codec.py`, plus untracked `__pycache__` directories from the test run.",
